    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0353" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4252: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-02T12:00:00-05:00">June 2, 1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        2:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. The President and the Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="32a"
                        xml:id="d287-f1"/> have both expressed the desire that in order to
                    accelerate the conclusion of the agreement regarding new fiscal arrangements the
                    negotiations should be carried on here the more so as the date of departure of
                    Dennis to the United States<anchor n="32b" xml:id="d287-f2"/> may be
                    delayed.</p>
                <p>Please cable how soon the Department will be ready to continue negotiations and
                    whether the above Haitian suggestion is agreeable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d287-f1" n="32a" xml:id="d287-f1-content">
                <p>Charles Fombrun became Minister for Foreign Affairs on May 15, 1941.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d287-f2" n="32b" xml:id="d287-f2-content">
                <p>Fernand Dennis, former Minister for Foreign Affairs, had been named Minister to
                    the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
